      "url": "https://x.com/TheWiseIC/status/2089078989503471674",
      "text": "@buggy_robot @ariaradnia How is $UBER or $FICO a value trap?\n\nUBER has an ecosystem that would take trillions to replicate their scale and they are transitioning into autonomy. It’s not a winner take all scenario, it never is. By your logic, Amazon should have went bankrupt because Alibaba, Temu and Shopify exist and have competitive pricing.\n\nFICO has a federally regualted moat still. I don’t see how it’s a value trap. \n\nAPP could be a value trap if the Apple ecosystem changes how data is shared with third party networks, but I don’t see that happening. But it’s a more realistic bear case than Uber being disrupted or FICO .",
      "original_text": "@buggy_robot @ariaradnia How is $UBER or $FICO a value trap?\n\nUBER has an ecosystem that would take trillions to replicate their scale and they are transitioning into autonomy. It’s not a winner take all scenario, it never is. By your logic, Amazon should have went bankrupt because Alibaba, Temu and Shopify exist and have competitive pricing.\n\nFICO has a federally regualted moat still. I don’t see how it’s a value trap. \n\nAPP could be a value trap if the Apple ecosystem changes how data is shared with third party networks, but I don’t see that happening. But it’s a more realistic bear case than Uber being disrupted or FICO .",
      "links": [],
      "translation_zh": "@buggy_robot @ariaradnia $UBER 或 $FICO 怎么会是价值陷阱？\n\nUBER 拥有一个生态系统，要复制他们的规模需要花费数万亿美元，而且他们正在向自动驾驶转型。这不是赢者通吃的局面，从来都不是。按你的逻辑，Amazon 本该破产，因为 Alibaba、Temu 和 Shopify 都存在，而且价格有竞争力。\n\nFICO 仍然有一个受联邦监管的护城河。我不明白它怎么会是价值陷阱。\n\n如果 Apple 生态系统改变与第三方网络共享数据的方式，APP 可能会成为价值陷阱，但我不认为这种事会发生。不过相比 Uber 被颠覆或 FICO，这个看空理由更现实。",
